> When you say the UNS could live in all 4 zones, is it unified? Is there a name space host in each zone with the same tags, or is there connectivity to a single host at level 1 or 2? Does the MQTT broker live at level 2 and every subscriber at every level has VPN to it? (Disclaimer; I am not a network genius)
> Thanks for the response Walker!
@patjdixon The unified namespace is built on technology (MQTT) that allows it to live in more than one place at a time -- you can have 100 brokers that all have the exact same namespace and values.  You can also create new brokers that only subscribe to a specific leaf node in the name space (and all of its children).  THE (the one true master) UNS generally lives in the Enterprise security zone in the Cisco drawing above, but with additional brokers at every other layer that may publish into the UNS or subscribe to a subset of the UNS.

