@Sam.E, I don't think the goal for OPC Foundation was "which is meant to compete with Sparkplug". When I was in OPC UA user group (it was not Pub/Sub group though), I never heard anything about SparkPlug in discussions. It might be to make easier to integrate with Microsoft's Event Hub, to integrate with Azure infrastructure in overall maybe. And at the same time given that OPC UA Pub/Sub implementation can be utilizing MQTT, potentially it can be integrated by any other, third party MQTT subscriber applications. 
I cannot eliminate that in the Pub/Sub user group SparkPlug was once considered, but not as a competing thing, just for suitability maybe, and I guess it was put aside as not conforming to all use cases the user group was focused on. Keep in mind that OPC UA user groups members have representatives from many companies around the world, and they all together put way more requirements to conform to, than just when you design something intended to use just by one or few companies.
I come to conclusion that while OPC Foundation is focused on creating a standard which can facilitate interoperability of applications from different vendors, most members of the community here at Discord are focused on keeping themselves free from using standards, more focused on making interoperable only limited set of applications used by them. Some kind of anti-standards rebels' movement. In that case there is no way these 2 groups will come to same common denominators. Refusing standards is not compatible with support of standards.

@john.harrington, in other topic we had discussion about polling at some level, and I think it was Rick who pointed that even at the lowest level sometimes data value can be received not by scanning, but by exception. So it might be more cases when OPC UA Servers receive data by exception for the primary data sources.
I think DNP-3 supports RBE for example. 
BTW, this is another myth that OPC UA Servers always use polling to get data from devices. But in fact I think they do that only if RBE is not supported by the device.

@Akshay, if your data is available over OPC UA, you can try also our ogamma Visual Logger for OPC, Community Edition is free forever for up to 64 variables. For one month after activation has all features. 
