@Indiecat here is the response from our Solutions Architect Evan McKee. 

Evan McKee
A question like this comes up a lot - "Now that I've structured my data and I understand how important it is to enforce that structure, what happens when I want it to change?" First, you are allowed to make multiple functional namespaces that are downstream of the UNS that have whatever different structure you need. Second, it's less accurate to say we're making global variables, and more accurate to say we are naming variables in accordance with their location in the namespace (which doesn't change very often). Thirdly, the statement "A lot of discipline is required to build business systems against the UNS and keep entropy at bay" is correct.

