Standard structure for the payload, and I can set the topic format.

@Don Pancoe Node red can read Sparkpluf pretty efficiently, the is a sparkplug node so no deed to go messing about with encoding and decoding to protobuf .

I'd say it absolutely is possible to use a bi-directional topic, by using different payload structures (akin to 'Interfaces' in software) to distinguish between a command and status, as well as other types of payloads as well. There are going to be tradeoffs either way you go: A) Two topics, or B) A single topic with different interfaces (i.e., payload structures).

Status Payload:
```json
{
    "Value": 1.0
}
```

Alternative Status Payload:
```json
{
    "Status": {
        "Value": 1.0
    }
}
```

Command Payload:
```json
{
    "Command": {
        "Value": 2.0
    }
}
```

