# What’s your biggest question about implementing a Unified Namespace in your organization?

@Brian McCarver  I think the best approach is that the Recipes are part of the UNS, but are not transported through the broker. I think you could get into issues, certainly at scale with a lot of retained topics, I think you would be better off having the recipes in a DB, and have a retained topic with the query to retrieve the latest recipe

Or if the legacy equipment is networked, have the recipe management system write to the CSV file the latest recipe, either on change, or on schedule.

Even where you have CSV files for Recipes, you can build a recipe management system and for new machines connect in the network format of your choice, but still have a function to export the latest recipes to the CSV files.

